<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquisate of Bodonitsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1204–1414</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marquisate of Bodonitsa was a small crusader state in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, created after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> to guard the pass of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thermopylae">Thermopylae</a>. Held by Italian families including the Pallavicini and later the Zorzi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, it acknowledged the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> as suzerains and fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1414.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marquisate-of-bodonitsa.jpg" alt="Marquisate of Bodonitsa" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mark Landon (photographed in 1990; digitized in 2021) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodonitsa_castle_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
